    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **51 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nThe response body is a MapStruct-generated `OwnerDto` (from `openapi.yml`), populated from the `Owner` entity's `@Transient` derived getters. To match that existing pattern I made three changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` readOnly string property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces the DTO field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` that splits the E.164 value into country code + national digits and groups the national digits in threes. It recognizes the app's two supported country codes (`+61` \u2192 2-digit CC, `+1` \u2192 NANP), falls back to a 2-digit code otherwise, and returns the raw value unchanged if it isn't in `+digits` form. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `@Mapping` expression wiring `getTelephoneDisplay()` onto the DTO, alongside the other derived-field mappings.\n\nThe new `Cp37Tests` passes (`telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`), and all 51 tests remain green.",
